WEBVTT

1
00:41:45.474 --> 00:41:50.394
So, it is wonderful to be together again.

2
00:41:50.394 --> 00:41:57.794
It is good to learn what God also wants to teach us about giving.

3
00:41:57.794 --> 00:41:59.994
Chris.

4
00:42:05.394 --> 00:42:09.914
Good morning. What a cozy atmosphere.

5
00:42:09.914 --> 00:42:12.114
Did you know that God is also cozy?

6
00:42:12.114 --> 00:42:17.314
He invented it. He thought of people then. Nice, isn't it?

7
00:42:17.314 --> 00:42:23.874
Hallelujah. We have a nice text this morning from Paul.

8
00:42:23.874 --> 00:42:27.634
Paul has so many beautiful texts, so actually you would want to cover them all,

9
00:42:27.634 --> 00:42:29.634
but you would need eternity for that.

10
00:42:29.634 --> 00:42:33.634
So we wanted to try to keep it a bit shorter.

11
00:42:33.634 --> 00:42:39.554
And this text says, God who gives seed to sow and bread to eat,

12
00:42:39.554 --> 00:42:47.554
will also give you seed and make it grow, so that your generosity will result in a rich harvest.

13
00:42:47.554 --> 00:42:52.554
You have become rich in every way so that you can be generous on every occasion.

14
00:42:52.554 --> 00:42:58.554
And your generosity will result in thanksgiving to God through us.

15
00:42:58.554 --> 00:43:03.554
And Paul writes here about the gifts that the Corinthians have given to the congregation in Jerusalem.

16
00:43:03.554 --> 00:43:08.554
They were actually doing very poorly. They had almost nothing.

17
00:43:08.554 --> 00:43:15.554
And Paul, with his shepherd's heart, also asks the people from Corinth to give.

18
00:43:15.554 --> 00:43:19.554
And that is something so beautiful that Paul gives here.

19
00:43:19.554 --> 00:43:25.554
And that those gifts also lead to thanksgiving to God in Jerusalem.

20
00:43:25.554 --> 00:43:32.554
So actually, by giving back, you worship God.

21
00:43:32.554 --> 00:43:35.554
You show that you want to bring back.

22
00:43:35.554 --> 00:43:39.554
And then it also leads to thanksgiving. How beautiful is this?

23
00:43:39.554 --> 00:43:43.554
And what he writes here also applies to us today.

24
00:43:43.554 --> 00:43:45.554
And let's zoom in on that for a moment.

25
00:43:45.554 --> 00:43:50.554
For this text clearly shows that God is our provider and that He wants to be there for us.

26
00:43:50.554 --> 00:43:56.554
He provides for everything. Both the seed, the bread, and also the harvest. Everything.

27
00:43:56.554 --> 00:44:02.554
And all wealth in every respect does not come from ourselves or myself.

28
00:44:02.554 --> 00:44:06.554
Everything I have, I have received from my Father. We used to have a song about that.

29
00:44:06.554 --> 00:44:12.554
And this text also shows that you may be rich in everything.

30
00:44:12.554 --> 00:44:16.554
In every respect, in every facet of our lives.

31
00:44:16.554 --> 00:44:19.554
Moreover, this is precisely the intention.

32
00:44:19.554 --> 00:44:24.554
It is God's intention that we become rich in every respect in our lives.

33
00:44:24.554 --> 00:44:28.554
If we are not rich, it is difficult to give.

34
00:44:29.554 --> 00:44:34.554
He has sent Jesus to bring us and life in abundance.

35
00:44:34.554 --> 00:44:37.554
So it is indeed the intention to be extremely rich.

36
00:44:37.554 --> 00:44:40.554
But, there is a caveat to it.

37
00:44:40.554 --> 00:44:42.554
And that caveat is also important.

38
00:44:42.554 --> 00:44:52.554
For at the same time, it is important that if you are rich, you remain humble or poor in spirit.

39
00:44:52.554 --> 00:44:55.554
Just as Matthew 5 teaches us.

40
00:44:55.554 --> 00:44:58.554
Where Jesus says that it is good to be poor in spirit.

41
00:44:58.554 --> 00:45:02.554
So on the one hand rich and on the other hand poor in spirit.

42
00:45:02.554 --> 00:45:08.554
And being poor in spirit actually means nothing other than knowing that and knowing it continually.

43
00:45:08.554 --> 00:45:13.554
That every form of wealth does not come from yourself, but comes from Him.

44
00:45:13.554 --> 00:45:15.554
That is being poor in spirit.

45
00:45:15.554 --> 00:45:19.554
And He has intended us to be rich.

46
00:45:19.554 --> 00:45:24.554
But it is also very important to realize that you are poor by yourself.

47
00:45:24.554 --> 00:45:28.554
And that everything you have truly comes from the Father.

48
00:45:28.554 --> 00:45:35.554
And precisely to remain poor in spirit when you are rich, that is what God has given the collection for.

49
00:45:35.554 --> 00:45:41.554
For do you know what it is? When we return to the Father what He has given us.

50
00:45:41.554 --> 00:45:43.554
Then we show this.

51
00:45:43.554 --> 00:45:45.554
And how beautiful is that?

52
00:45:45.554 --> 00:45:49.554
So we may give back from all the wealth that we have.

53
00:45:49.554 --> 00:45:53.554
We truly live in a rich piece of earth.

54
00:45:53.554 --> 00:45:59.554
The three percent richest people on earth is really true.

55
00:45:59.554 --> 00:46:01.554
May we return.

56
00:46:01.554 --> 00:46:06.554
Why? So that His house grows and that we can also distribute.

57
00:46:06.554 --> 00:46:11.554
But at the same time God will bless you again for that generosity.

58
00:46:11.554 --> 00:46:13.554
And that is actually a circle.

59
00:46:13.554 --> 00:46:15.554
And it goes on and on.

60
00:46:15.554 --> 00:46:17.554
And your faith will grow because you may receive more.

61
00:46:17.554 --> 00:46:21.554
But then you also know that you may bring back more.

62
00:46:21.554 --> 00:46:26.554
And this is what God wants to do. He wants to make us strong as his church.

63
00:46:26.554 --> 00:46:31.554
That we can provide for people and that we can provide in the house of God.

64
00:46:31.554 --> 00:46:39.554
What in turn, actually like we are all gathered here, now enjoying the worship and the presence of God.

65
00:46:39.554 --> 00:46:42.554
This is what we can give as the church.

66
00:46:42.554 --> 00:46:45.554
And there are also all kinds of costs and expenses needed for that.

67
00:46:45.554 --> 00:46:49.554
Let us think about the fact that in this way we may be partners of God.

68
00:46:49.554 --> 00:46:52.554
And at the same time, God will make us richer and richer.

69
00:46:52.554 --> 00:46:55.554
And I want to thank God for that.

70
00:46:55.554 --> 00:46:58.554
And perhaps it is nice to do that together as we stand up.

71
00:46:58.554 --> 00:47:01.554
And that we thank God for the riches he has given.

72
00:47:01.554 --> 00:47:05.554
Father, thank you. You are good. You are such a loving father.

73
00:47:05.554 --> 00:47:08.554
And you want us to be able to handle much.

74
00:47:08.554 --> 00:47:12.554
That you want to entrust us with much. Why?

75
00:47:12.554 --> 00:47:15.554
Because we grow. Because we will receive even more in the future.

76
00:47:15.554 --> 00:47:18.554
Even in the new world, we will receive even more.

77
00:47:18.554 --> 00:47:24.554
Lord, all the money of this world. It is not even change for the groceries you would do.

78
00:47:24.554 --> 00:47:29.554
Lord, it is real. You are so great and you are so powerful and you have so much to give us.

79
00:47:29.554 --> 00:47:32.554
Let us then do well on this earth and want to do good.

80
00:47:32.554 --> 00:47:37.554
Knowing that we are poor in spirit. And therefore may receive the riches of Christ.

81
00:47:37.554 --> 00:47:41.554
And I pray this over us as a church. So that our church may grow.

82
00:47:41.554 --> 00:47:46.554
And that many souls may be added in the name of King Jesus. Amen.

83
00:47:47.554 --> 00:47:51.554
APPLAUSE

84
00:47:56.554 --> 00:48:03.554
I have a few fun things. Namely, the summer camps are coming up.

85
00:48:03.554 --> 00:48:09.554
Namely the children's camp and the youth camp. And you don't want to miss that.

86
00:48:09.554 --> 00:48:16.554
So young people, make sure you have signed up. Check with your parents. Ask them about it. Pull on their ears.

87
00:48:16.554 --> 00:48:21.554
Sign up. Everyone must be registered by August 1st.

88
00:48:21.554 --> 00:48:24.554
Parents, sign up your children. It is so important.

89
00:48:24.554 --> 00:48:31.554
I myself also went to children's camps from the church when I was younger. And it is amazing.

90
00:48:31.554 --> 00:48:35.554
Later I also had the opportunity to help organize those children's camps.

91
00:48:36.554 --> 00:48:40.554
It is wonderful to see what God does through those children.

92
00:48:40.554 --> 00:48:45.554
And you shouldn't think that, okay, this is what God does at the adult level.

93
00:48:45.554 --> 00:48:48.554
And children's level is then that.

94
00:48:49.554 --> 00:48:54.554
Often it is the case that children have such great faith. And they are so open to everything.

95
00:48:54.554 --> 00:48:58.554
That if this is the adult level, for children it is there.

96
00:48:59.554 --> 00:49:04.554
God does so much for children, for young people.

97
00:49:04.554 --> 00:49:09.554
You know, you need God. Even today at school. You need God.

98
00:49:09.554 --> 00:49:16.554
And you can't do without Him. So parents, climb onto that website.

99
00:49:16.554 --> 00:49:20.554
The links are on the website. There you can register your children.

100
00:49:20.554 --> 00:49:26.554
Also make sure to pay by August 1st. The leaders will find it handy that it is settled.

101
00:49:26.554 --> 00:49:32.554
And of course, men, we do not forget you. Because Real Men Camp is in September.

102
00:49:32.554 --> 00:49:36.554
And the same actually applies to you.

103
00:49:36.554 --> 00:49:40.554
You simply cannot lead your life today without God.

104
00:49:40.554 --> 00:49:45.554
You have never been able to do that. But it is happening very quickly these days.

105
00:49:45.554 --> 00:49:49.554
With all sorts of difficult things or strange times in the world.

106
00:49:49.554 --> 00:49:53.554
You need God. You need God. You need God.

107
00:49:53.554 --> 00:49:57.554
So men, if you want to be a strong man in Christ, sign up.

108
00:49:57.554 --> 00:50:03.554
Because that is where you can specifically get your teaching for men as well.

109
00:50:03.554 --> 00:50:08.554
And also hear from others how do you live together with God.

110
00:50:08.554 --> 00:50:12.554
But fine, go to that website and arrange it.

111
00:50:12.554 --> 00:50:18.554
Bram, the honor is yours. Shall we welcome him for a moment?

112
00:50:24.554 --> 00:50:28.554
And thank you, Bram.

113
00:50:28.554 --> 00:50:33.554
Thank you. Good morning.

114
00:50:33.554 --> 00:50:38.554
I see a lot of familiar faces. I see a lot of gaps.

115
00:50:38.554 --> 00:50:42.554
I assume that all those gaps mean that there are people on vacation.

116
00:50:42.554 --> 00:50:47.554
Maybe there are also guests here who are on vacation now.

117
00:50:47.554 --> 00:50:50.554
A very warm welcome.

118
00:50:51.554 --> 00:50:53.554
Take a seat.

119
00:50:53.554 --> 00:50:55.554
And I say take a seat.

120
00:50:55.554 --> 00:50:58.554
And what I mean by that is also.

121
00:50:58.554 --> 00:51:01.554
You know, let us open our hearts.

122
00:51:01.554 --> 00:51:06.554
I am going to explain something today.

123
00:51:06.554 --> 00:51:09.554
To bring something up from the Bible.

124
00:51:09.554 --> 00:51:15.554
The essence of which is that we all need to understand it ourselves.

125
00:51:15.554 --> 00:51:16.554
We need to grasp it ourselves.

126
00:51:16.554 --> 00:51:18.554
You have to see it.

127
00:51:18.554 --> 00:51:22.554
Once you see what God's plan is, you can never unsee it.

128
00:51:22.554 --> 00:51:25.554
If you understand what I mean.

129
00:51:25.554 --> 00:51:27.554
But that is something personal.

130
00:51:27.554 --> 00:51:32.554
That is something that must be revealed in your own heart by the Holy Spirit.

131
00:51:32.554 --> 00:51:40.554
And that plan of God begins right at the front of the Bible.

132
00:51:40.554 --> 00:51:46.554
And by the way, it ends right at the back of the Bible and points to the eternity that is yet to come.

133
00:51:46.554 --> 00:51:50.554
God has given us the Bible.

134
00:51:50.554 --> 00:51:53.554
Not primarily as a history book.

135
00:51:53.554 --> 00:52:00.554
But primarily to show who He is.

136
00:52:00.554 --> 00:52:03.554
And what is actually His idea with people.

137
00:52:03.554 --> 00:52:06.554
What is His idea with a world.

138
00:52:06.554 --> 00:52:09.554
What is His idea with you and with me.

139
00:52:09.554 --> 00:52:17.554
For it sometimes concerns very big things and at the same time it concerns very personal and intimate things.

140
00:52:17.554 --> 00:52:19.554
About how we function.

141
00:52:19.554 --> 00:52:21.554
How we are meant to be.

142
00:52:21.554 --> 00:52:25.554
How we are made.

143
00:52:25.554 --> 00:52:28.554
And that starts right at the beginning of the Bible.

144
00:52:28.554 --> 00:52:33.554
And today we will read many pieces from the Bible.

145
00:52:33.554 --> 00:52:39.554
Because actually, everything is just there.

146
00:52:39.554 --> 00:52:46.554
And it actually does not depend on explanation at all.

147
00:52:46.554 --> 00:52:52.554
But you have to see it, and it must be revealed in your heart.

148
00:52:52.554 --> 00:53:02.554
And our Bible starts with creation, with paradise.

149
00:53:02.554 --> 00:53:11.554
And there the core is laid of what it is all about.

150
00:53:11.554 --> 00:53:19.554
Do you know that story about the apple?

151
00:53:19.554 --> 00:53:24.554
That apple in paradise where everything went wrong. Do you know that story?

152
00:53:24.554 --> 00:53:28.554
And that one bite from the apple that is called the fall into sin.

153
00:53:28.554 --> 00:53:30.554
Do you know that story?

154
00:53:30.554 --> 00:53:33.554
Well, let me tell you, none of it is true.

155
00:53:35.554 --> 00:53:37.554
There was no apple.

156
00:53:37.554 --> 00:53:43.554
And it was about much more than just a bite from a piece of fruit.

157
00:53:46.554 --> 00:53:48.554
Let's start there then.

158
00:53:48.554 --> 00:53:51.554
Let's take a look at what it says.

159
00:53:51.554 --> 00:53:55.554
From Genesis 2 starting at verse 5.

160
00:53:56.554 --> 00:54:03.554
In the beginning, there were no shrubs on the earth at all.

161
00:54:03.554 --> 00:54:06.554
There was not even any grass growing.

162
00:54:06.554 --> 00:54:09.554
For the Lord had not yet caused it to rain.

163
00:54:09.554 --> 00:54:14.554
There was also no one to work the ground.

164
00:54:14.554 --> 00:54:20.554
A mist rose from the earth, which kept the ground moist.

165
00:54:21.554 --> 00:54:28.554
When the Lord God made the heavens and the earth, he also made man.

166
00:54:28.554 --> 00:54:37.554
He made him from the dust of the ground and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.

167
00:54:37.554 --> 00:54:43.554
Thus man became a living being.

168
00:54:43.554 --> 00:54:47.554
This word life, that is what we will talk about.

169
00:54:48.554 --> 00:54:55.554
Man became a living being through the breath of life from God.

170
00:54:55.554 --> 00:54:58.554
The Lord God also made a garden in Eden.

171
00:54:58.554 --> 00:55:02.554
The word Eden means beautiful.

172
00:55:04.554 --> 00:55:07.554
Apparently, that was in the east.

173
00:55:09.554 --> 00:55:14.554
I am not entirely sure if people in Japan still had this in the east.

174
00:55:15.554 --> 00:55:19.554
I believe that is not the core.

175
00:55:19.554 --> 00:55:22.554
God made a garden in Eden.

176
00:55:22.554 --> 00:55:26.554
There he placed the man whom he had made.

177
00:55:26.554 --> 00:55:31.554
The Lord God also ensured that all kinds of trees grew there.

178
00:55:31.554 --> 00:55:34.554
Beautiful trees with delicious fruits.

179
00:55:34.554 --> 00:55:42.554
In the middle of the garden stood the tree of eternal life and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.

180
00:55:45.554 --> 00:55:52.554
In other verses, we read that Adam and Eve enjoyed the garden.

181
00:55:52.554 --> 00:55:57.554
And that they walked with God in the evening coolness.

182
00:55:57.554 --> 00:56:03.554
So during the day it was quite warm and the evening coolness was delightful and refreshing.

183
00:56:05.554 --> 00:56:09.554
I can already see the people in Spain longing for the evening coolness.

184
00:56:09.554 --> 00:56:10.554
Or not?

185
00:56:12.554 --> 00:56:17.554
This is a description of exactly what we seek when we want to go on vacation.

186
00:56:18.554 --> 00:56:27.554
Somewhere within us, we have that knowledge of what a good, a beautiful, a perfect environment is.

187
00:56:27.554 --> 00:56:36.554
And we all recognize that longing for paradise where there is harmony.

188
00:56:37.554 --> 00:56:40.554
Where man walks with God.

189
00:56:41.554 --> 00:56:43.554
And they talk to each other.

190
00:56:43.554 --> 00:56:45.554
And look here.

191
00:56:46.554 --> 00:56:48.554
Yes, Adam.

192
00:56:49.554 --> 00:56:51.554
I made him too.

193
00:56:51.554 --> 00:56:53.554
What do you want to call him?

194
00:56:53.554 --> 00:56:57.554
Well, yes, that says, yes.

195
00:56:57.554 --> 00:56:59.554
What shall I call this one?

196
00:56:59.554 --> 00:57:01.554
You know what?

197
00:57:02.554 --> 00:57:04.554
This is Lion.

198
00:57:04.554 --> 00:57:07.554
And somewhere we all see a picture.

199
00:57:08.554 --> 00:57:14.554
And the other one is called Paradise Bird.

200
00:57:14.554 --> 00:57:17.554
I don't know where that name comes from.

201
00:57:18.554 --> 00:57:21.554
Paradise is not doing nothing.

202
00:57:21.554 --> 00:57:24.554
For there is already talk about cultivating the earth.

203
00:57:26.554 --> 00:57:33.554
Paradise is being active and seeing the full fruit of what you do.

204
00:57:33.554 --> 00:57:38.554
And having the satisfaction that something beautiful has happened.

205
00:57:38.554 --> 00:57:43.554
And everything works and functions.

206
00:57:44.554 --> 00:57:49.554
There is no longer the toil of work, but the fruit of work.

207
00:57:53.554 --> 00:57:56.554
God made man alive.

208
00:57:57.554 --> 00:58:00.554
What does it mean to be alive?

209
00:58:01.554 --> 00:58:05.554
God made man alive by His breath of life.

210
00:58:06.554 --> 00:58:11.554
There is the word Breath. The word Ruach is used here.

211
00:58:12.554 --> 00:58:16.554
We do not know that in our language.

212
00:58:16.554 --> 00:58:26.554
But in Hebrew and Greek, there are words that have a very rich and versatile meaning.

213
00:58:26.554 --> 00:58:28.554
Ruach is breath.

214
00:58:28.554 --> 00:58:31.554
It is also simply wind.

215
00:58:33.554 --> 00:58:37.554
But Ruach is also inspiration.

216
00:58:37.554 --> 00:58:40.554
It is also spirit.

217
00:58:40.554 --> 00:58:46.554
The Ruach of God is also the Holy Spirit, for God is holy.

218
00:58:49.554 --> 00:58:52.554
So man received.

219
00:58:52.554 --> 00:58:56.554
Man was made from clay.

220
00:58:56.554 --> 00:58:59.554
He became a body.

221
00:58:59.554 --> 00:59:01.554
Still now.

222
00:59:01.554 --> 00:59:07.554
And man received a spiritual, a divine life.

223
00:59:10.554 --> 00:59:13.554
Further in verse 15.

224
00:59:17.554 --> 00:59:24.554
The Lord, the Lord God placed man in the garden of Eden to take care of the garden.

225
00:59:24.554 --> 00:59:26.554
And He warned him.

226
00:59:26.554 --> 00:59:31.554
You may eat from all the trees in the garden, as much as you want.

227
00:59:31.554 --> 00:59:35.554
But do not eat from the tree of knowledge of good and evil.

228
00:59:35.554 --> 00:59:39.554
For on the day that you eat from it, you shall surely die.

229
00:59:41.554 --> 00:59:44.554
Everything is there.

230
00:59:44.554 --> 00:59:47.554
God provides for everything.

231
00:59:47.554 --> 00:59:49.554
This is His plan.

232
00:59:49.554 --> 00:59:51.554
This has been His intention.

233
00:59:51.554 --> 00:59:53.554
Everything good.

234
00:59:53.554 --> 00:59:55.554
Healthy.

235
00:59:55.554 --> 01:00:01.554
Work and see the consequences and see the fruit.

236
01:00:02.554 --> 01:00:07.554
Sow a handful of grain and all the grain will sprout.

237
01:00:07.554 --> 01:00:10.554
There is no storm that flattens it.

238
01:00:10.554 --> 01:00:13.554
It invents a nice machine.

239
01:00:13.554 --> 01:00:16.554
And that machine just works.

240
01:00:16.554 --> 01:00:19.554
For we are made creative.

241
01:00:21.554 --> 01:00:24.554
But there are limits.

242
01:00:24.554 --> 01:00:29.554
God wants us to respect Him as God.

243
01:00:29.554 --> 01:00:32.554
To know Him.

244
01:00:32.554 --> 01:00:38.554
To accept Him as God.

245
01:00:42.554 --> 01:00:45.554
There are limits.

246
01:00:45.554 --> 01:00:48.554
There is such a thing as the knowledge of good and evil.

247
01:00:48.554 --> 01:00:50.554
And we will come to that.

248
01:00:50.554 --> 01:00:53.554
For on the day that you eat of it, you shall surely die.

249
01:00:53.554 --> 01:00:55.554
It is stated very explicitly.

250
01:00:55.554 --> 01:00:58.554
On the day that you eat of it.

251
01:00:58.554 --> 01:01:01.554
We will see what happened.

252
01:01:01.554 --> 01:01:04.554
Chapter 3, verse 1.

253
01:01:04.554 --> 01:01:06.554
The serpent.

254
01:01:06.554 --> 01:01:10.554
He was more cunning than any other wild animal that the Lord God had made.

255
01:01:10.554 --> 01:01:13.554
It was the devil who spoke through the serpent.

256
01:01:13.554 --> 01:01:16.554
And he said to the woman.

257
01:01:16.554 --> 01:01:22.554
Did God really say that you shall not eat of any tree in the garden?

258
01:01:25.554 --> 01:01:27.554
That is not true at all.

259
01:01:27.554 --> 01:01:28.554
The woman answered.

260
01:01:28.554 --> 01:01:31.554
We may eat the fruit of all the trees in the garden.

261
01:01:31.554 --> 01:01:35.554
Only not from the fruits of the tree that stands in the middle of the garden.

262
01:01:35.554 --> 01:01:37.554
God has said that.

263
01:01:37.554 --> 01:01:39.554
You may not eat from that tree.

264
01:01:39.554 --> 01:01:42.554
You must not even touch it, or you will die.

265
01:01:44.554 --> 01:01:47.554
But the serpent said to the woman.

266
01:01:48.554 --> 01:01:51.554
You will not surely die.

267
01:01:51.554 --> 01:01:55.554
God knows that when you eat from it, your eyes will be opened.

268
01:01:55.554 --> 01:01:59.554
You will be like God, knowing good and evil.

269
01:02:02.554 --> 01:02:06.554
Then the woman was very eager to eat from the fruits of the tree.

270
01:02:06.554 --> 01:02:08.554
They looked so attractive.

271
01:02:08.554 --> 01:02:12.554
She wanted to eat from it so badly because she would become wise.

272
01:02:12.554 --> 01:02:15.554
She picked a fruit from the tree and ate it.

273
01:02:15.554 --> 01:02:18.554
She also gave one to her husband, who was with her.

274
01:02:18.554 --> 01:02:20.554
He ate the fruit.

275
01:02:21.554 --> 01:02:27.554
This is the account of the greatest disaster that has ever happened in humanity.

276
01:02:29.554 --> 01:02:37.554
This has had more consequences than volcanic eruptions, than floods, than you can imagine.

277
01:02:37.554 --> 01:02:44.554
Earthquakes, we have seen earthquakes where tens of thousands of people have died.

278
01:02:44.554 --> 01:02:48.554
That means there were many more people nearby.

279
01:02:48.554 --> 01:02:52.554
That means there were many more people injured or severely injured.

280
01:02:52.554 --> 01:02:54.554
Perhaps disabled for life.

281
01:02:54.554 --> 01:02:57.554
This is much, much worse.

282
01:03:01.554 --> 01:03:03.554
Let's see what happens.

283
01:03:03.554 --> 01:03:05.554
What is the devil whispering?

284
01:03:08.554 --> 01:03:11.554
You can't have anything from God, right?

285
01:03:14.554 --> 01:03:16.554
That is a scandalous lie.

286
01:03:16.554 --> 01:03:18.554
God says, I have made everything for you.

287
01:03:18.554 --> 01:03:22.554
You can use everything, just stay away from that one.

288
01:03:24.554 --> 01:03:26.554
You can't have anything from God, right?

289
01:03:27.554 --> 01:03:29.554
And do you know what the point is?

290
01:03:31.554 --> 01:03:33.554
Eve gives an answer.

291
01:03:33.554 --> 01:03:38.554
Eve answers, no, we may eat from all the trees.

292
01:03:40.554 --> 01:03:45.554
But from that one tree, we must not touch or eat.

293
01:03:45.554 --> 01:03:47.554
Wait a minute, who talked about touching?

294
01:03:49.554 --> 01:03:52.554
God said, you may not eat from that tree.

295
01:03:52.554 --> 01:03:58.554
And suddenly Eve says, but we must not touch or eat from it.

296
01:04:04.554 --> 01:04:08.554
You know, when you engage in a discussion with the devil,

297
01:04:09.554 --> 01:04:16.554
it is so easy to go along with a certain line of reasoning.

298
01:04:19.554 --> 01:04:23.554
Actually, she is already giving a bit away.

299
01:04:27.554 --> 01:04:29.554
You must not drink from that one.

300
01:04:30.554 --> 01:04:32.554
You certainly can't have anything.

301
01:04:32.554 --> 01:04:34.554
This is a dangerous thing.

302
01:04:38.554 --> 01:04:40.554
Do you feel what is happening?

303
01:04:40.554 --> 01:04:42.554
Do you sense it?

304
01:04:45.554 --> 01:04:49.554
It goes in the direction of, God is strict.

305
01:04:49.554 --> 01:04:54.554
God acts, God sets things down.

306
01:04:54.554 --> 01:04:56.554
That will only get worse.

307
01:05:03.554 --> 01:05:06.554
The serpent then says to the woman,

308
01:05:07.554 --> 01:05:10.554
you will not surely die.

309
01:05:11.554 --> 01:05:15.554
Again, God is made a liar.

310
01:05:16.554 --> 01:05:19.554
God says on the day that you eat, you will die.

311
01:05:19.554 --> 01:05:22.554
The serpent says, no way, not at all.

312
01:05:25.554 --> 01:05:29.554
And then a seed is planted.

313
01:05:31.554 --> 01:05:35.554
For God wants to withhold something.

314
01:05:36.554 --> 01:05:39.554
There is something that God has not told you.

315
01:05:41.554 --> 01:05:43.554
If God has not told you something,

316
01:05:43.554 --> 01:05:46.554
if He has not revealed something,

317
01:05:46.554 --> 01:05:48.554
then that is up to Him.

318
01:05:48.554 --> 01:05:51.554
We have no opinion about that at all.

319
01:05:53.554 --> 01:05:57.554
For if you eat from it,

320
01:05:57.554 --> 01:06:00.554
then you will see the truth.

321
01:06:02.554 --> 01:06:05.554
Oh, how attractive that sounds.

322
01:06:06.554 --> 01:06:07.554
Right?

323
01:06:07.554 --> 01:06:09.554
Truth is good, isn't it?

324
01:06:10.554 --> 01:06:12.554
Right?

325
01:06:15.554 --> 01:06:18.554
Then you will have more knowledge.

326
01:06:18.554 --> 01:06:21.554
Knowledge is good, isn't it? Right?

327
01:06:22.554 --> 01:06:25.554
What could possibly be wrong with knowledge?

328
01:06:25.554 --> 01:06:27.554
How you use it can be dangerous.

329
01:06:27.554 --> 01:06:29.554
But knowledge is good, isn't it?

330
01:06:30.554 --> 01:06:33.554
You will be like God.

331
01:06:33.554 --> 01:06:35.554
And God does not want that.

332
01:06:35.554 --> 01:06:38.554
God does not want you to be like God.

333
01:06:38.554 --> 01:06:41.554
But then you will be like God.

334
01:06:46.554 --> 01:06:50.554
And we all fall into that trap.

335
01:06:51.554 --> 01:06:53.554
All of us.

336
01:06:54.554 --> 01:06:56.554
All of us.

337
01:06:57.554 --> 01:07:03.554
We all think from time to time that we know better.

338
01:07:03.554 --> 01:07:05.554
Or not sometimes?

339
01:07:08.554 --> 01:07:10.554
Humans fall into it.

340
01:07:10.554 --> 01:07:12.554
Being like God.

341
01:07:14.554 --> 01:07:16.554
When I look at our society,

342
01:07:16.554 --> 01:07:19.554
everyone has their own truth.

343
01:07:21.554 --> 01:07:24.554
For everyone is like God.

344
01:07:27.554 --> 01:07:31.554
The essence of sin is not

345
01:07:31.554 --> 01:07:34.554
having taken the cookie from your mother's jar.

346
01:07:35.554 --> 01:07:38.554
The essence of sin is

347
01:07:39.554 --> 01:07:43.554
the person, I, determining it myself.

348
01:07:44.554 --> 01:07:47.554
I know better.

349
01:07:49.554 --> 01:07:53.554
So I determine what is good and evil.

350
01:07:54.554 --> 01:07:58.554
For I have eaten from the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.

351
01:07:59.554 --> 01:08:01.554
Right?

352
01:08:03.554 --> 01:08:07.554
Man determines his own moral framework.

353
01:08:07.554 --> 01:08:10.554
Isn't that what we see in society as a whole?

354
01:08:11.554 --> 01:08:14.554
Man strives for his own,

355
01:08:14.554 --> 01:08:16.554
then I will use difficult words,

356
01:08:16.554 --> 01:08:19.554
but difficult words, you know,

357
01:08:20.554 --> 01:08:25.554
to be like God is to be sovereign.

358
01:08:25.554 --> 01:08:30.554
Man strives and demands in this society

359
01:08:30.554 --> 01:08:33.554
his own sovereignty.

360
01:08:33.554 --> 01:08:35.554
I must be able to do it myself.

361
01:08:36.554 --> 01:08:39.554
No one tells me what is good and evil.

362
01:08:39.554 --> 01:08:41.554
I determine that myself.

363
01:08:42.554 --> 01:08:44.554
Moral autonomy.

364
01:08:44.554 --> 01:08:47.554
In all ethical and moral aspects of life.

365
01:08:47.554 --> 01:08:50.554
I will decide that myself.

366
01:08:52.554 --> 01:08:54.554
We all want freedom.

367
01:08:55.554 --> 01:08:57.554
Did the other one know?

368
01:08:58.554 --> 01:09:00.554
All those things sound so beautiful.

369
01:09:00.554 --> 01:09:02.554
What is wrong with freedom?

370
01:09:03.554 --> 01:09:05.554
Well?

371
01:09:06.554 --> 01:09:09.554
We all strive for freedom.

372
01:09:09.554 --> 01:09:11.554
And there are a whole lot of things

373
01:09:11.554 --> 01:09:14.554
that people need to break free from and be free from,

374
01:09:14.554 --> 01:09:17.554
which are also a result of that misery

375
01:09:17.554 --> 01:09:20.554
that we have brought upon ourselves.

376
01:09:22.554 --> 01:09:25.554
But where is the line between freedom and debauchery?

377
01:09:28.554 --> 01:09:30.554
We want freedom.

378
01:09:32.554 --> 01:09:34.554
We want independence.

379
01:09:36.554 --> 01:09:40.554
And so we have become individuals in this society.

380
01:09:45.554 --> 01:09:48.554
We must have our own opinion about everything.

381
01:09:49.554 --> 01:09:52.554
And if we want it, then it must be now.

382
01:09:54.554 --> 01:09:58.554
And so we are as humans and as a society

383
01:09:59.554 --> 01:10:01.554
lost.

384
01:10:01.554 --> 01:10:03.554
For this is lostness.

385
01:10:04.554 --> 01:10:08.554
We have become lost in a sea of infinitely many opinions.

386
01:10:08.554 --> 01:10:10.554
And where is the support?

387
01:10:11.554 --> 01:10:13.554
Where are the boundaries?

388
01:10:14.554 --> 01:10:17.554
How do we know if we have meaningful opinions?

389
01:10:22.554 --> 01:10:26.554
The human in this way is the human as God.

390
01:10:29.554 --> 01:10:31.554
Completely individual.

391
01:10:31.554 --> 01:10:33.554
Autonomous.

392
01:10:33.554 --> 01:10:35.554
Independent.

393
01:10:35.554 --> 01:10:37.554
Sovereign.

394
01:10:38.554 --> 01:10:41.554
There are people who have thought about this.

395
01:10:41.554 --> 01:10:44.554
There is a world-famous philosopher, Jean-Paul Sartre.

396
01:10:45.554 --> 01:10:49.554
He is the founder of a philosophical movement called existentialism.

397
01:10:52.554 --> 01:10:55.554
These are people who look at life.

398
01:10:56.554 --> 01:10:58.554
I sometimes compare that to Ecclesiastes.

399
01:10:58.554 --> 01:11:01.554
Ecclesiastes looked at life and the Bible says

400
01:11:01.554 --> 01:11:04.554
he considered life under the sun.

401
01:11:04.554 --> 01:11:06.554
So he considered earthly life.

402
01:11:06.554 --> 01:11:09.554
Ecclesiastes at least came to the conclusion

403
01:11:09.554 --> 01:11:11.554
there is a sense of eternity.

404
01:11:11.554 --> 01:11:12.554
There is a God.

405
01:11:12.554 --> 01:11:15.554
But he simply looked at life on this earth.

406
01:11:15.554 --> 01:11:17.554
This man comes to the conclusion

407
01:11:17.554 --> 01:11:20.554
without having a sense of God.

408
01:11:20.554 --> 01:11:22.554
Without having an interest in God.

409
01:11:22.554 --> 01:11:25.554
For he looks at life on this earth.

410
01:11:25.554 --> 01:11:30.554
Man is only what he makes of himself.

411
01:11:32.554 --> 01:11:37.554
That is the deep, ultimate consequence of

412
01:11:38.554 --> 01:11:40.554
man wanting to be like God.

413
01:11:41.554 --> 01:11:43.554
For if you want to be like God

414
01:11:43.554 --> 01:11:46.554
you are also left to yourself.

415
01:11:46.554 --> 01:11:49.554
And so we get in our society

416
01:11:49.554 --> 01:11:50.554
this story

417
01:11:50.554 --> 01:11:53.554
You must become who you are.

418
01:11:56.554 --> 01:12:00.554
But if you are only what you make of yourself

419
01:12:00.554 --> 01:12:02.554
then you must also make something of yourself.

420
01:12:02.554 --> 01:12:05.554
You must become who you are.

421
01:12:05.554 --> 01:12:07.554
But if you already are that, how are you supposed to become it?

422
01:12:07.554 --> 01:12:09.554
I don't understand that.

423
01:12:09.554 --> 01:12:14.554
And you must also be alone, let that sink in.

424
01:12:14.554 --> 01:12:19.554
A person is only what he makes of himself.

425
01:12:19.554 --> 01:12:23.554
Only what you make of yourself.

426
01:12:26.554 --> 01:12:29.554
So I must become who I truly am

427
01:12:29.554 --> 01:12:30.554
but I must also shape myself

428
01:12:30.554 --> 01:12:32.554
and only I make something of myself.

429
01:12:33.554 --> 01:12:36.554
What a loneliness.

430
01:12:37.554 --> 01:12:40.554
What a lostness.

431
01:12:43.554 --> 01:12:49.554
And so the question of who am I can no longer be answered.

432
01:12:49.554 --> 01:12:56.554
And we live in a society

433
01:12:56.554 --> 01:13:01.554
where the idea is that everything is malleable.

434
01:13:02.554 --> 01:13:05.554
If we are like God

435
01:13:05.554 --> 01:13:09.554
then we think we have influence over everything

436
01:13:09.554 --> 01:13:10.554
and can make everything

437
01:13:10.554 --> 01:13:11.554
and can change everything

438
01:13:11.554 --> 01:13:14.554
and can shape everything to our will.

439
01:13:17.554 --> 01:13:20.554
Then you can apply it everywhere.

440
01:13:20.554 --> 01:13:23.554
About how society is structured.

441
01:13:23.554 --> 01:13:26.554
About what you can achieve in your life.

442
01:13:26.554 --> 01:13:28.554
And then suddenly it is indeed about

443
01:13:28.554 --> 01:13:31.554
yes but you can achieve anything in life.

444
01:13:31.554 --> 01:13:33.554
Yes.

445
01:13:35.554 --> 01:13:39.554
And if I have to achieve everything in life myself

446
01:13:41.554 --> 01:13:43.554
and it doesn't work out

447
01:13:47.554 --> 01:13:50.554
then I am to blame

448
01:13:51.554 --> 01:13:54.554
and I end up in a depression.

449
01:13:54.554 --> 01:13:56.554
Or someone else is to blame

450
01:13:56.554 --> 01:13:58.554
and then I get angry.

451
01:13:58.554 --> 01:14:02.554
Or whatever.

452
01:14:03.554 --> 01:14:06.554
And of course there is much more to say about depression.

453
01:14:06.554 --> 01:14:08.554
And of course there is much more to say about anger.

454
01:14:08.554 --> 01:14:12.554
But notice how that basic identity here

455
01:14:12.554 --> 01:14:15.554
is the core of all misery.

456
01:14:15.554 --> 01:14:17.554
When a person is left to themselves

457
01:14:17.554 --> 01:14:19.554
then they are deeply lonely.

458
01:14:19.554 --> 01:14:23.554
And then you either scream out the loneliness

459
01:14:23.554 --> 01:14:25.554
or numb it.

460
01:14:25.554 --> 01:14:27.554
And then you start blaming someone else.

461
01:14:27.554 --> 01:14:30.554
or blame yourself if it doesn't quite work out.

462
01:14:33.554 --> 01:14:38.554
This is our lostness.

463
01:14:38.554 --> 01:14:40.554
We are as human beings and as humanity

464
01:14:40.554 --> 01:14:43.554
in a state of being lost.

465
01:14:43.554 --> 01:14:46.554
We are no longer in that state of life

466
01:14:46.554 --> 01:14:48.554
that God intended.

467
01:14:48.554 --> 01:14:52.554
But we have come into a state of existence.

468
01:14:52.554 --> 01:14:55.554
We have come into a state of survival.

469
01:14:55.554 --> 01:14:58.554
Just as Adam and Eve began

470
01:14:58.554 --> 01:15:03.554
in that state of rich and spacious life together with God.

471
01:15:03.554 --> 01:15:05.554
Life with a capital letter.

472
01:15:05.554 --> 01:15:10.554
And after their wrong choices

473
01:15:10.554 --> 01:15:12.554
they continued to live.

474
01:15:12.554 --> 01:15:15.554
But life became a struggle.

475
01:15:15.554 --> 01:15:18.554
And one son killed the other.

476
01:15:23.554 --> 01:15:28.554
And we must be delivered from that.

477
01:15:28.554 --> 01:15:33.554
We must be saved from our lostness.

478
01:15:39.554 --> 01:15:41.554
And here is the moment

479
01:15:41.554 --> 01:15:45.554
that something very fundamental must change.

480
01:15:47.554 --> 01:15:49.554
Galatians 2.

481
01:15:49.554 --> 01:15:51.554
Galatians 2 verse 20.

482
01:15:52.554 --> 01:15:54.554
There Paul suddenly says something.

483
01:15:54.554 --> 01:15:57.554
Something very special.

484
01:15:57.554 --> 01:15:59.554
Something very unusual.

485
01:15:59.554 --> 01:16:01.554
Then he says.

486
01:16:02.554 --> 01:16:04.554
Then he talks about

487
01:16:04.554 --> 01:16:07.554
how he experiences his own life at that moment.

488
01:16:07.554 --> 01:16:08.554
And then he says.

489
01:16:08.554 --> 01:16:12.554
For I have been crucified with Christ, and yet I live.

490
01:16:12.554 --> 01:16:17.554
That is because it is no longer my own self that lives.

491
01:16:17.554 --> 01:16:20.554
But Christ lives in me.

492
01:16:20.554 --> 01:16:23.554
When we wanted to be like God

493
01:16:23.554 --> 01:16:25.554
we seized power

494
01:16:25.554 --> 01:16:29.554
and we began to place our own self at the center.

495
01:16:29.554 --> 01:16:33.554
And we began to live our own self.

496
01:16:33.554 --> 01:16:35.554
Our own self on the throne.

497
01:16:35.554 --> 01:16:37.554
As if we were sovereign.

498
01:16:37.554 --> 01:16:40.554
And oh what misery that

499
01:16:40.554 --> 01:16:44.554
beautiful promise of the devil has caused.

500
01:16:46.554 --> 01:16:48.554
But he was right.

501
01:16:48.554 --> 01:16:50.554
Man has become like God.

502
01:16:51.554 --> 01:16:53.554
Do you know?

503
01:16:56.554 --> 01:16:58.554
How do I say that?

504
01:17:00.554 --> 01:17:03.554
When the devil mirrors something

505
01:17:03.554 --> 01:17:05.554
it can sound very attractive.

506
01:17:05.554 --> 01:17:09.554
And still many of those concepts sound appealing.

507
01:17:09.554 --> 01:17:12.554
But woe to you if you receive it.

508
01:17:12.554 --> 01:17:14.554
For he has mirrored something beautiful

509
01:17:14.554 --> 01:17:17.554
but never explained the consequences.

510
01:17:17.554 --> 01:17:20.554
You find the consequences in the Word of God.

511
01:17:22.554 --> 01:17:24.554
Here is the liberation.

512
01:17:24.554 --> 01:17:27.554
Here Paul says

513
01:17:29.554 --> 01:17:34.554
I live, and that is because it is no longer my own self

514
01:17:34.554 --> 01:17:37.554
but Christ lives in me.

515
01:17:38.554 --> 01:17:41.554
No longer my own self

516
01:17:41.554 --> 01:17:43.554
but Christ.

517
01:17:44.554 --> 01:17:47.554
How did that happen?

518
01:17:47.554 --> 01:17:50.554
What is he talking about here?

519
01:17:50.554 --> 01:17:53.554
For now he has restored

520
01:17:53.554 --> 01:17:56.554
the situation as it was.

521
01:17:56.554 --> 01:17:59.554
God, as sovereign God.

522
01:17:59.554 --> 01:18:01.554
God as Lord.

523
01:18:01.554 --> 01:18:04.554
He who provides for everything.

524
01:18:04.554 --> 01:18:06.554
He who has good in store for us in everything.

525
01:18:06.554 --> 01:18:09.554
He who knows what we need in everything

526
01:18:09.554 --> 01:18:11.554
and has provided for everything.

527
01:18:11.554 --> 01:18:14.554
God.

528
01:18:14.554 --> 01:18:16.554
He who lives in me, he says.

529
01:18:16.554 --> 01:18:19.554
Christ lives in me.

530
01:18:19.554 --> 01:18:22.554
Then let's go to the gospel.

531
01:18:22.554 --> 01:18:25.554
John 1.

532
01:18:25.554 --> 01:18:28.554
And John 1

533
01:18:28.554 --> 01:18:32.554
actually gives a bird's eye view of the entire history of the world

534
01:18:32.554 --> 01:18:34.554
and it starts back at Genesis

535
01:18:34.554 --> 01:18:37.554
where we also began just now.

536
01:18:38.554 --> 01:18:41.554
In the beginning, the Word was there.

537
01:18:41.554 --> 01:18:44.554
Jesus was already there. God was already there.

538
01:18:44.554 --> 01:18:47.554
The Word was with God

539
01:18:47.554 --> 01:18:50.554
and the Word was God Himself.

540
01:18:50.554 --> 01:18:52.554
The Word is Jesus.

541
01:18:52.554 --> 01:18:54.554
In the beginning was the Word with God.

542
01:18:54.554 --> 01:18:56.554
Jesus was with God in the beginning.

543
01:18:56.554 --> 01:18:58.554
All things were made through the Word.

544
01:18:58.554 --> 01:19:01.554
Truly everything that exists, exists

545
01:19:01.554 --> 01:19:03.554
because the Word made it.

546
01:19:03.554 --> 01:19:06.554
In the Word was life

547
01:19:06.554 --> 01:19:09.554
and the life was the light for people.

548
01:19:11.554 --> 01:19:13.554
Everything began with God.

549
01:19:13.554 --> 01:19:15.554
God was there.

550
01:19:15.554 --> 01:19:17.554
Jesus was there.

551
01:19:17.554 --> 01:19:20.554
Everything is perfectly, good, fully made by Him.

552
01:19:20.554 --> 01:19:22.554
And Jesus was already there.

553
01:19:22.554 --> 01:19:24.554
He already existed. God.

554
01:19:24.554 --> 01:19:26.554
As Debbie said earlier.

555
01:19:26.554 --> 01:19:27.554
God in heaven.

556
01:19:27.554 --> 01:19:30.554
Who chose

557
01:19:30.554 --> 01:19:33.554
to create that wonderfully beautiful earth.

558
01:19:33.554 --> 01:19:36.554
That earth which we have made a mess of.

559
01:19:36.554 --> 01:19:38.554
Where lostness has come.

560
01:19:38.554 --> 01:19:41.554
And then Jesus chose

561
01:19:41.554 --> 01:19:45.554
to live out of that comfortable heaven

562
01:19:45.554 --> 01:19:47.554
in the midst of lostness

563
01:19:47.554 --> 01:19:49.554
to go live.

564
01:19:54.554 --> 01:19:56.554
The light shines in the darkness

565
01:19:56.554 --> 01:19:58.554
and the darkness has not overcome it.

566
01:19:58.554 --> 01:20:01.554
The darkness is that lostness I was talking about.

567
01:20:01.554 --> 01:20:03.554
God sent a man.

568
01:20:03.554 --> 01:20:05.554
John the Baptist.

569
01:20:05.554 --> 01:20:08.554
He had to tell the people about the light.

570
01:20:08.554 --> 01:20:11.554
Through him they would be able to believe in the light.

571
01:20:12.554 --> 01:20:14.554
He was not the light himself, but he came

572
01:20:14.554 --> 01:20:16.554
to tell about the light.

573
01:20:18.554 --> 01:20:20.554
John the Baptist points to Jesus.

574
01:20:20.554 --> 01:20:22.554
Explains it.

575
01:20:22.554 --> 01:20:26.554
And step by step this explanation is developed here.

576
01:20:27.554 --> 01:20:31.554
John the Baptist speaks about Jesus who is coming.

577
01:20:31.554 --> 01:20:33.554
Jesus who brings the light

578
01:20:33.554 --> 01:20:35.554
in that darkness of lostness.

579
01:20:38.554 --> 01:20:40.554
Verse 9.

580
01:20:40.554 --> 01:20:42.554
For he who was the true light

581
01:20:42.554 --> 01:20:44.554
would almost come.

582
01:20:45.554 --> 01:20:49.554
And it gives light to every person.

583
01:20:51.554 --> 01:20:54.554
And now it becomes personal.

584
01:20:54.554 --> 01:20:59.554
Now suddenly from the great creation,

585
01:20:59.554 --> 01:21:02.554
from the great God who makes everything,

586
01:21:03.554 --> 01:21:06.554
all things made by him.

587
01:21:06.554 --> 01:21:08.554
Suddenly,

588
01:21:10.554 --> 01:21:12.554
now I am lost where I was,

589
01:21:12.554 --> 01:21:14.554
he gives light to every person.

590
01:21:14.554 --> 01:21:18.554
It is possible for every person.

591
01:21:20.554 --> 01:21:22.554
He had made the earth

592
01:21:22.554 --> 01:21:24.554
and has now come to the earth himself.

593
01:21:25.554 --> 01:21:27.554
But the people did not recognize him.

594
01:21:27.554 --> 01:21:29.554
Many people have not realized at all

595
01:21:29.554 --> 01:21:31.554
who Jesus actually is.

596
01:21:31.554 --> 01:21:32.554
And that is nothing new either.

597
01:21:32.554 --> 01:21:34.554
Because that is still the case today.

598
01:21:35.554 --> 01:21:37.554
He came to the people he himself had made.

599
01:21:37.554 --> 01:21:39.554
Can you imagine?

600
01:21:39.554 --> 01:21:42.554
God has made us all himself.

601
01:21:42.554 --> 01:21:45.554
And he came to us.

602
01:21:49.554 --> 01:21:51.554
But they did not want to believe in him.

603
01:21:52.554 --> 01:21:54.554
Oh, how painful.

604
01:21:56.554 --> 01:22:00.554
But to all the people who do believe in him,

605
01:22:00.554 --> 01:22:04.554
he has given the right to become children of God.

606
01:22:05.554 --> 01:22:08.554
The right here is a mandate.

607
01:22:08.554 --> 01:22:11.554
You have received all the possibilities.

608
01:22:11.554 --> 01:22:13.554
You still have to make use of them.

609
01:22:14.554 --> 01:22:18.554
They are born again.

610
01:22:19.554 --> 01:22:23.554
They are not born of flesh and blood.

611
01:22:23.554 --> 01:22:26.554
As our body is born.

612
01:22:26.554 --> 01:22:28.554
Not by the desires of a man.

613
01:22:28.554 --> 01:22:31.554
We all know what preceded this.

614
01:22:31.554 --> 01:22:34.554
But their spirit is born of God.

615
01:22:35.554 --> 01:22:46.554
Here something so fundamental is explained.

616
01:22:47.554 --> 01:22:51.554
So in the beginning we are born as babies.

617
01:22:52.554 --> 01:22:56.554
We are born in the natural way.

618
01:22:57.554 --> 01:22:59.554
We call that life.

619
01:23:01.554 --> 01:23:04.554
The Bible actually calls that only half life.

620
01:23:04.554 --> 01:23:06.554
That is an existence.

621
01:23:08.554 --> 01:23:14.554
Here it is spoken that their spirit is born of God.

622
01:23:14.554 --> 01:23:16.554
For those who believe.

623
01:23:16.554 --> 01:23:18.554
For those who are born again.

624
01:23:18.554 --> 01:23:20.554
That is being born again.

625
01:23:20.554 --> 01:23:23.554
Spirit born of God.

626
01:23:23.554 --> 01:23:26.554
For us. Individually.

627
01:23:27.554 --> 01:23:31.554
That is living according to the meaning of God.

628
01:23:31.554 --> 01:23:34.554
That is living with a capital letter.

629
01:23:34.554 --> 01:23:36.554
This is God providing for life.

630
01:23:36.554 --> 01:23:43.554
God has made everything possible and provides everything from Him.

631
01:23:44.554 --> 01:23:49.554
If you think, I don't understand that, then you are not alone.

632
01:23:50.554 --> 01:23:57.554
There was also a scholar among the Jewish people at the time this happened.

633
01:23:57.554 --> 01:24:00.554
And he didn't understand it either.

634
01:24:00.554 --> 01:24:04.554
So fortunately we also have his account.

635
01:24:04.554 --> 01:24:06.554
In John 3.

636
01:24:08.554 --> 01:24:12.554
There was a Pharisee named Nicodemus.

637
01:24:13.554 --> 01:24:15.554
John 3 verses.

638
01:24:16.554 --> 01:24:18.554
He was one of the Jewish leaders.

639
01:24:19.554 --> 01:24:22.554
One night he went to Jesus and said to him.

640
01:24:22.554 --> 01:24:27.554
Teacher, we know that you are a teacher who has come from God.

641
01:24:28.554 --> 01:24:31.554
For no one can do the wonders that you do.

642
01:24:32.554 --> 01:24:35.554
And that can only happen if God is with him.

643
01:24:36.554 --> 01:24:39.554
That is a nice introduction.

644
01:24:40.554 --> 01:24:42.554
He says to Jesus.

645
01:24:42.554 --> 01:24:44.554
You must come from God.

646
01:24:44.554 --> 01:24:46.554
That is true.

647
01:24:46.554 --> 01:24:48.554
But Jesus does not respond to that.

648
01:24:49.554 --> 01:24:51.554
Jesus answered, listen carefully.

649
01:24:52.554 --> 01:24:54.554
He goes to his heart.

650
01:24:56.554 --> 01:25:01.554
I say that you can only belong to the kingdom of God if you are born again.

651
01:25:02.554 --> 01:25:04.554
So it is indeed important.

652
01:25:04.554 --> 01:25:08.554
You can only belong to the kingdom of God if you are born again.

653
01:25:10.554 --> 01:25:13.554
Nicodemus asked, how can you be born when you are old?

654
01:25:15.554 --> 01:25:19.554
You cannot enter your mother's womb again and be born a second time, can you?

655
01:25:21.554 --> 01:25:22.554
Yes?

656
01:25:24.554 --> 01:25:26.554
Logical man, I think then.

657
01:25:26.554 --> 01:25:27.554
Logical man.

658
01:25:27.554 --> 01:25:28.554
But he does not get it.

659
01:25:29.554 --> 01:25:31.554
He does not grasp what Jesus is talking about.

660
01:25:31.554 --> 01:25:33.554
Jesus answered him, listen carefully.

661
01:25:33.554 --> 01:25:34.554
I tell you.

662
01:25:34.554 --> 01:25:39.554
You can only enter the kingdom of God if you are born of water and of spirit.

663
01:25:39.554 --> 01:25:40.554
Otherwise not.

664
01:25:42.554 --> 01:25:45.554
From a human, human life is born.

665
01:25:47.554 --> 01:25:50.554
But from God's spirit, spiritual life is born.

666
01:25:51.554 --> 01:25:54.554
So it is not strange that I say you are born again.

667
01:25:55.554 --> 01:25:58.554
So it is not strange that I say you all must be born again.

668
01:25:58.554 --> 01:25:59.554
It is not strange.

669
01:26:00.554 --> 01:26:05.554
Jesus says, I have a very logical story for you.

670
01:26:06.554 --> 01:26:11.554
If you only exist in the natural, you will not go beyond the natural.

671
01:26:12.554 --> 01:26:15.554
And then you are in that state of being lost.

672
01:26:15.554 --> 01:26:18.554
But you need to be born again.

673
01:26:18.554 --> 01:26:22.554
And born with a life from God.

674
01:26:23.554 --> 01:26:25.554
With a spiritual life.

675
01:26:25.554 --> 01:26:28.554
And that can only come from God.

676
01:26:30.554 --> 01:26:33.554
The wind blows, verse 8, wherever it wishes.

677
01:26:33.554 --> 01:26:37.554
You hear it, but you do not know where it comes from or where it goes.

678
01:26:37.554 --> 01:26:41.554
So it is with everyone who is born of God's spirit.

679
01:26:41.554 --> 01:26:44.554
You cannot measure it with a ruler.

680
01:26:44.554 --> 01:26:47.554
You cannot put it on a scale and weigh it.

681
01:26:47.554 --> 01:26:51.554
You cannot buy a little spiritual life at the butcher's.

682
01:26:51.554 --> 01:26:52.554
No.

683
01:26:53.554 --> 01:26:56.554
It is life.

684
01:26:56.554 --> 01:26:59.554
You cannot name life.

685
01:26:59.554 --> 01:27:06.554
The life with God, the life with the Holy Spirit.

686
01:27:06.554 --> 01:27:10.554
That is an incredible, clear, distinct reality.

687
01:27:10.554 --> 01:27:13.554
Just like you see and feel the wind.

688
01:27:13.554 --> 01:27:15.554
The reality is there.

689
01:27:15.554 --> 01:27:18.554
But can you point out where that wind comes from?

690
01:27:19.554 --> 01:27:21.554
From the top of the tower?

691
01:27:21.554 --> 01:27:22.554
No.

692
01:27:24.554 --> 01:27:27.554
But you know it comes from the source of God.

693
01:27:29.554 --> 01:27:33.554
Nicodemus asked Jesus, how can someone be born of God's Spirit?

694
01:27:43.554 --> 01:27:44.554
How?

695
01:27:44.554 --> 01:27:46.554
Jesus will explain it like this.

696
01:27:46.554 --> 01:27:49.554
But you need to understand the question first.

697
01:27:49.554 --> 01:27:52.554
How are we naturally born?

698
01:27:52.554 --> 01:27:57.554
Well, something has preceded it between dad and mom.

699
01:27:57.554 --> 01:28:01.554
And then a baby grows.

700
01:28:01.554 --> 01:28:05.554
And at a certain moment, the baby is born.

701
01:28:07.554 --> 01:28:09.554
How are we spiritually born?

702
01:28:09.554 --> 01:28:11.554
Did we choose to be naturally born?

703
01:28:11.554 --> 01:28:12.554
No.

704
01:28:13.554 --> 01:28:18.554
Being born is something that happens to you.

705
01:28:18.554 --> 01:28:20.554
But something did precede it.

706
01:28:20.554 --> 01:28:28.554
What precedes our spiritual birth is, as we just read, accepting Jesus.

707
01:28:28.554 --> 01:28:31.554
And believing.

708
01:28:31.554 --> 01:28:35.554
Believing is, I place my trust in it.

709
01:28:35.554 --> 01:28:44.554
Believing is not, I have no idea what it's about, but I'll just do something.

710
01:28:44.554 --> 01:28:46.554
It will be fine.

711
01:28:46.554 --> 01:28:56.554
Believing is not so much, there is this enormous black hole and I just jump in without any idea.

712
01:28:56.554 --> 01:29:00.554
For believing is believing in God, believing is believing in Jesus.

713
01:29:00.554 --> 01:29:05.554
He has been revealed and He has described Himself and shown Himself.

714
01:29:05.554 --> 01:29:11.554
Believing is indeed letting go of the self.

715
01:29:11.554 --> 01:29:13.554
Making that choice.

716
01:29:15.554 --> 01:29:20.554
Trusting in Christ is also called conversion.

717
01:29:20.554 --> 01:29:25.554
It is stepping aside from the throne of the self.

718
01:29:26.554 --> 01:29:30.554
Acknowledging God as God.

719
01:29:30.554 --> 01:29:33.554
Acknowledging Him as Lord.

720
01:29:33.554 --> 01:29:36.554
Jesus explains this further here.

721
01:29:36.554 --> 01:29:39.554
John 3 verse 13.

722
01:29:39.554 --> 01:29:43.554
No one has ever gone to heaven except the one who came from heaven.

723
01:29:43.554 --> 01:29:46.554
Actually, I know it, I come from there myself.

724
01:29:46.554 --> 01:29:49.554
I, the Son of Man.

725
01:29:49.554 --> 01:29:51.554
I have come from there.

726
01:29:51.554 --> 01:29:55.554
And just as Moses lifted up a serpent in the wilderness,

727
01:29:55.554 --> 01:29:59.554
so must the Son of Man be lifted up.

728
01:29:59.554 --> 01:30:04.554
Everyone who believes in him will not perish but have eternal life.

729
01:30:04.554 --> 01:30:06.554
The Son of Man, Jesus himself.

730
01:30:06.554 --> 01:30:09.554
Believing in him, having eternal life.

731
01:30:09.554 --> 01:30:15.554
Having eternal life does not begin at the gate of heaven.

732
01:30:15.554 --> 01:30:17.554
Yes, here we do our best.

733
01:30:18.554 --> 01:30:20.554
We do not know how it...

734
01:30:20.554 --> 01:30:22.554
We do our best.

735
01:30:22.554 --> 01:30:24.554
Yes, sometimes things go wrong.

736
01:30:24.554 --> 01:30:26.554
Then we arrive at the gate of heaven after death.

737
01:30:26.554 --> 01:30:28.554
And there stands Peter.

738
01:30:28.554 --> 01:30:32.554
And Peter then says, yes, let's take a look.

739
01:30:32.554 --> 01:30:35.554
Yes, you may enter.

740
01:30:35.554 --> 01:30:38.554
That is not eternal life.

741
01:30:38.554 --> 01:30:41.554
Eternal life has already begun here.

742
01:30:41.554 --> 01:30:45.554
Eternal life has already begun through that regeneration.

743
01:30:45.554 --> 01:30:48.554
For life from God is eternal.

744
01:30:48.554 --> 01:30:50.554
Life from God does not change.

745
01:30:50.554 --> 01:30:52.554
So that begins here.

746
01:30:52.554 --> 01:30:54.554
And it continues eternally.

747
01:30:54.554 --> 01:30:56.554
Our body must go through that death.

748
01:30:56.554 --> 01:30:59.554
It said so.

749
01:30:59.554 --> 01:31:01.554
Our life is already eternal.

750
01:31:01.554 --> 01:31:04.554
If we have that regeneration.

751
01:31:04.554 --> 01:31:07.554
Okay, I will go back to the text.

752
01:31:11.554 --> 01:31:14.554
Everyone who believes in him will not die,

753
01:31:14.554 --> 01:31:16.554
but will have eternal life.

754
01:31:16.554 --> 01:31:18.554
For God loves people so much.

755
01:31:18.554 --> 01:31:21.554
That he has given his only son to them.

756
01:31:21.554 --> 01:31:23.554
Everyone.

757
01:31:23.554 --> 01:31:24.554
Everyone.

758
01:31:24.554 --> 01:31:26.554
Again an individual choice.

759
01:31:26.554 --> 01:31:29.554
Do you see how the plan is for the people?

760
01:31:29.554 --> 01:31:33.554
But everyone is individual.

761
01:31:33.554 --> 01:31:35.554
For everyone personally.

762
01:31:39.554 --> 01:31:42.554
Everyone who believes in him will not perish,

763
01:31:42.554 --> 01:31:44.554
but will have eternal life.

764
01:31:44.554 --> 01:31:49.554
For God did not send his Son into the world to condemn people.

765
01:31:51.554 --> 01:31:53.554
God is not angry.

766
01:31:55.554 --> 01:31:59.554
God is not angry.

767
01:32:03.554 --> 01:32:05.554
But to save people.

768
01:32:08.554 --> 01:32:11.554
God feels pain for the lostness.

769
01:32:12.554 --> 01:32:20.554
God can be furious about the misery that happens in this world.

770
01:32:20.554 --> 01:32:22.554
And he can also be sad about it.

771
01:32:22.554 --> 01:32:25.554
But he is not angry with you.

772
01:32:27.554 --> 01:32:29.554
For he came to save.

773
01:32:31.554 --> 01:32:34.554
Everyone who believes in him is not condemned.

774
01:32:34.554 --> 01:32:35.554
Do you see that?

775
01:32:35.554 --> 01:32:37.554
Everyone who believes in him is not condemned.

776
01:32:37.554 --> 01:32:39.554
You will not be turned away at the gate.

777
01:32:40.554 --> 01:32:43.554
But everyone who does not believe is already condemned.

778
01:32:43.554 --> 01:32:45.554
Here lies the choice.

779
01:32:48.554 --> 01:32:51.554
For he has not believed in the only Son of God.

780
01:32:52.554 --> 01:32:57.554
Here is the opportunity to escape the lostness.

781
01:32:59.554 --> 01:33:01.554
And do you see the mirror?

782
01:33:01.554 --> 01:33:03.554
Do you see the mirror that the Bible has here?

783
01:33:04.554 --> 01:33:10.554
In paradise, God began to give fully beautiful life to humanity, to Adam.

784
01:33:11.554 --> 01:33:13.554
He breathed the spirit into him.

785
01:33:14.554 --> 01:33:17.554
And there was a good and complete life.

786
01:33:17.554 --> 01:33:19.554
And it was fantastic.

787
01:33:21.554 --> 01:33:24.554
And through the choice, as you all have made,

788
01:33:24.554 --> 01:33:33.554
life was transformed into an existence, into mere survival.

789
